CMEPS: cache PIO decompositions instead of rebuilding them per FieldBundle

APPLIES ON TOP OF cmeps-mediator-restart-io.patch AND cmeps-restart-timers.patch
(with the ESMF_TraceRegionEnter/Exit import that the first version of the timer
patch was missing).

Measured with those trace regions, ACCESS-OM3 8 km, 8216 PETs, 1-day segment:

  MED:(med_phases_restart_write)              326.58
    med_io_FB_initdecomp      Count 12        274.40   84.0%   22.87 s/bundle
    med_io_FB_freedecomp      Count 12         14.14    4.3%
    med_io_close              Count  1          6.85    2.1%
    med_io_FB_darray          Count 12          0.76    0.2%
    residual (untimed)                         30.35    9.3%

pio_initdecomp is 84% of the mediator restart write; the pio_write_darray loop
that moves the 25 GB is 0.76 s. Build plus free is 288.5 s of 326.6 s.

The min/max columns show why: on one PET initdecomp is 5.91 s and freedecomp is
320.30 s; on another 276.39 s and 11.66 s. They are collectives and whoever
arrives early waits in the next one, so the pair is the cost.

The 12 FieldBundles in this restart differ in nothing pio_initdecomp depends on:
ATM, ICE, OCN and ROF share one ESMFmesh at 4320 x 3672. Cache the decomposition,
keyed on the PIO base type, the global dimensions and this PET's local degrees of
freedom compared element-wise.

Collective safety is the delicate part -- a lookup that leaves PETs disagreeing
about whether to call the collective pio_initdecomp is a hang, not a wrong
answer. Each PET reduces its local hit index with one ESMF_VMAllReduce, sending
(hit, -hit) with MAX so a single collective yields both the maximum and the
minimum; the hit is taken only when they agree and are positive. Any
disagreement, including two PETs hitting different slots, falls through to a
build on every PET.

io_desc_t is a single integer handle, so returning a copy cannot alias anything
later freed, and the decomposition belongs to the iosystem rather than to a file.
The per-call pio_freedecomp is removed; med_io_finalize (called from
med_finalize, outside the maintask guard because it is collective) releases
everything and logs hit and build counts. The med_io_FB_freedecomp trace region
goes with it.

EXPECTED: initdecomp 274.40 -> 22.87 s and freedecomp 14.14 -> 0, so about
-266 s on the restart write, 326.6 s -> roughly 61 s, about a third of the 1-day
wall clock. The med_io_FB_initdecomp region is kept around the cache lookup so
the profile shows this directly -- its Count stays at 12 (the region wraps the
lookup as well as any build); the TIME is the signal.

Touches mediator/med_io_mod.F90 and mediator/med.F90.

